          "instructions": "Clear, measured, and instructor-ready.",
          "text": "The full reasoning chain is compact: group bits, map a symbol, modulate orthogonal carriers, pass through the channel, synchronize, filter, sample, decide, and decode. To debug a link, compare evidence at each boundary. Verify the bit mapping, inspect carrier frequency and timing, plot the received constellation, measure error-vector magnitude, and compare transmitted with recovered bits. This stepwise view turns an abstract modulation formula into a practical engineering workflow."
